<td>NIPCO WARRI</td>\n                <td>₦1,690.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>PRUDENT OGHARA</td>\n                <td>₦1,690.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>AFRICAN TERMINAL</td>\n                <td>₦1,660.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>T.TIME</td>\n                <td>₦1,655.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>WOSBAB</td>\n                <td>₦1,670.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>TMDK</td>\n                <td>₦1,670.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>INTERGRATED</td>\n                <td>₦1,660.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>IBETO</td>\n                <td>₦1,665.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n\n        </table>\n\n        <br>\n        \n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            Market News\n        </h2>\n        \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Liberia Joins West Africa's Energy Leaders at OTL Africa 2026\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    The Liberia Petroleum Products Retailers Union (LIPPRU) has confirmed its participation in the 20th anniversary edition of OTL Africa Downstream Energy Week. The event is scheduled for 25–30 October 2026 at the Oriental Hotel, Lagos, under the theme \"Secure Energy, Share Prosperity\" LIPPRu President Prince Tambah Nyumah said the invitation gives Liberia the opportunity to showcase developments in its petroleum sector.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/liberia-joins-west-africas-energy-leaders-at-otl-africa-2026\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    FG Resets Deepwater Profit Split to 70:30 to Lure Fresh Investment\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    The Federal Government has introduced a new fiscal incentive that could give fresh deepwater oil projects a significantly more attractive starting position. Under the new Profit Oil Reset mechanism, an approved greenfield development will not inherit the more burdensome profit-oil sharing level reached by existing production within the same contract area.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/fg-resets-deepwater-profit-split-to-7030-to-lure-fresh-investment\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Strait of Hormuz Tanker Traffic Slumps as U.S.-Iran Faceoff Lingers\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Only five commodity vessels crossed the strategic waterway on Saturday, while no crossings were scheduled for Sunday. The figures compare with 31 tanker crossings recorded over the previous weekend. Despite the sharp decline in visible tanker traffic, crude prices have remained below their earlier highs.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/strait-of-hormuz-tanker-traffic-slumps-as-us-iran-faceoff-lingers\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Why Oil Prices Aren’t Rising Despite the Strait of Hormuz Crisis\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Oil prices have remained relatively subdued despite the prolonged disruption around the Strait of Hormuz. Brent crude was trading around $88.52 a barrel on Friday, down 1.7 percent since the start of August. The International Energy Agency has significantly lowered its outlook for global oil demand this year.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/why-oil-prices-arent-rising-despite-the-strait-of-hormuz-crisis\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    FG Launches Crude Trading Platform to Boost Refinery Supply\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    The Federal Government has introduced an automated crude oil trading platform designed to connect crude producers, regulators, refineries and oil marketers in a single marketplace. The platform will allow participants to conduct live transactions and coordinate crude allocation, pricing, sales and delivery.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/fg-launches-crude-trading-platform-to-boost-refinery-supply\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n\n        </body>\n\n        </html>\n        "
